From: Paul Schuldesz <paulschuldesz@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a8xx: invalidate CCHE on pagetable switch (FP6 candidate)

The pagetable switch in a6xx_set_pagetable() ends with a CACHE_INVALIDATE
event ("be sure there isn't anything lingering in that part of the GPU").
On gen8 userspace (Mesa freedreno and turnip) emits a separate
CP_CCHE_INVALIDATE next to CACHE_INVALIDATE, which suggests the event does
not cover the CCHE there. Emit it (after a WFI, see Mesa commit
5fcde4d65d8f "freedreno: Fix CP_CCHE_INVALIDATE not being applied at the
right point") on a8xx so that no context can sample lines cached under the
previous context's pagetable.

Unverified candidate for the FP6 "text turns into boxes" bug, which hits
the shell and several apps at once. Not upstream.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
@@ -327,6 +327,18 @@
 	OUT_PKT7(ring, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
 	OUT_RING(ring, CACHE_INVALIDATE);
 
+	/*
+	 * FP6 candidate: on a8xx the CCHE is not covered by the CACHE_INVALIDATE
+	 * event (userspace emits CP_CCHE_INVALIDATE separately on gen8), so lines
+	 * cached under the previous context's pagetable could survive the switch.
+	 * CP_CCHE_INVALIDATE is a plain register write underneath; WFI first so
+	 * it applies after the previous context's work (mesa 5fcde4d65d8f).
+	 */
+	if (adreno_is_a8xx(adreno_gpu)) {
+		OUT_PKT7(ring, CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE, 0);
+		OUT_PKT7(ring, CP_CCHE_INVALIDATE, 0);
+	}
+
 	if (!sysprof) {
 		u32 reg_status = adreno_is_a8xx(adreno_gpu) ?
 			REG_A8XX_RBBM_PERFCTR_SRAM_INIT_STATUS :
